    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Edamame is soy in its most whole-food form. The pods containing young soybeans are a snack or starter, first popularized in East Asia. Soybeans naturally contain a class of phytoestrogens called isoflavones. People hear “estrogen” in “phytoestrogens” and assume that means soy has estrogen-like effects. This is not necessarily true. Estrogen has positive effects in some tissues and potentially negative effects in others. Visit the edamame </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/edamame/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">topic page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for more information.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4>Recipe: Edamame Guacamole</h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/edamame-guacamole/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-88043 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/edamame-guac-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/edamame-guac-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/edamame-guac-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/edamame-guac-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/edamame-guac-1536x1536.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/edamame-guac-2048x2048.jpg 2048w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/edamame-guac-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/edamame-guac-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/edamame-guac-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/edamame-guac-540x540.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Feeling creative? Try this new take on guacamole. Blend shelled edamame with avocados and your favorite salt-free seasonings, and enjoy it as a spread or a dip for fresh veggies. Get the free recipe </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/edamame-guacamole/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and visit our </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CakSTRkAxXv/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Instagram</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for a video on how it’s made.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4>New Items on NutritionFacts.org</h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-88049\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/webinars-sq.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/webinars-sq.png 946w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/webinars-sq-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/webinars-sq-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/webinars-sq-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/webinars-sq-540x540.png 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>I’ve been doing live webinars for the past four years, covering topics like fasting, SIBO, and potatoes. The live presentations allow for participants to be the first to hear the information and get answers to their questions right on the spot. The videos I go over in the webinars, as you may know, are always eventually available for free on ​​NutritionFacts.org, but we have just started putting the full webinar recording online, too, after the videos have been released on the site. So, not only can you view all of the videos related to a topic in one place, you can access the Q&amp;A that happened live during the webinar itself! See for yourself</span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/webinars/\"> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here on the webinar pages</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">I regularly update my list of optimum nutrients—the vitamins and minerals we should ensure we get enough of. See my latest on our new </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/optimum-nutrient-recommendations/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Optimum Nutrient Recommendations webpage</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4>Volunteer Spotlight: Sheila and David Krawchuk</h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-88053\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/pxl-20220614-232010001-1024x1378.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"192\" height=\"259\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/pxl-20220614-232010001-1024x1378.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/pxl-20220614-232010001-960x1292.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/pxl-20220614-232010001-768x1033.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/pxl-20220614-232010001-1142x1536.jpg 1142w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/pxl-20220614-232010001-1522x2048.jpg 1522w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/pxl-20220614-232010001-1200x1615.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/pxl-20220614-232010001-720x969.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/pxl-20220614-232010001-540x727.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/pxl-20220614-232010001-scaled.jpg 1903w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 192px) 100vw, 192px\"/>We are both incredibly happy to help spread the whole food, plant-based message through the work of NutritionFacts and love being volunteers. Sheila reviews and uploads videos to YouTube and Vimeo, and Dave embeds Chinese and English subtitles in videos for social media and helps prepare Spanish-language blogs.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Dave’s favorite food is Brussels sprouts and his favorite recipe is a ginger-chipotle-chocolate-maca frozen nice cream. Sheila’s favorite food is an apple. (She was extremely happy that the breast cancer chapter in </span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Not to Die</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> noted the benefits of apples.) Her favorite recipe is frozen no-eggnog nice cream—a recipe she made up consisting of 2 bananas, 2 teaspoons of Ceylon cinnamon, ¼ teaspoon of cloves, some grinds of fresh nutmeg, a teaspoon of vanilla, and a splash of soy milk.</span></p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4>Thank You to All of Our Volunteers</h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-88047 size-large\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/volunteers-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/volunteers-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/volunteers-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/volunteers-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/volunteers-1536x1536.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/volunteers-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/volunteers-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/volunteers-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/volunteers-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/volunteers.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/>Are you interested in helping spread the word about NutritionFacts? Check out some quick actions you can take on our </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/volunteer/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">volunteer page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, or consider </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">making a donation</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> this summer!</span></p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4>Top Three Videos</h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-for-hair-growth/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-86240\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"roasted pumpkin seeds on cloth over black surface\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-03-food-for-hair-growth.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-for-hair-growth/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Food for Hair Growth</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> – Hot peppers, soy foods, and pumpkin seeds may help with hair loss.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-86259\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-05-are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"assortment of nuts over grey surface\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-05-are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-05-are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-05-are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-05-are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-05-are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-05-are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-05-are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-05-are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/05/58-05-are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/are-the-health-benefits-of-nuts-limited-to-those-eating-bad-diets/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Are the Health Benefits of Nuts Limited to Those Eating Bad Diets?</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> – Do nut eaters live longer simply because they swap in protein from plants in place of animal protein?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-85011\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/57-26-animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"a bowl filled with grains and beans\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/57-26-animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/57-26-animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/57-26-animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/57-26-animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/57-26-animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/57-26-animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/57-26-animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/57-26-animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/03/57-26-animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/animal-protein-vs-plant-based-protein/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Animal Protein vs. Plant-Based Protein</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> – I discuss a public health case for modernizing the definition of protein quality.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4>Healthy Eating Game</h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-88035\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/07/dd-sq.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"199\"/>Our friends at AppStop.io created a fun app that educates and encourages players to make healthy eating choices based on the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dining-by-traffic-light-green-is-for-go-red-is-for-stop/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">traffic light system</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> described in </span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Not to Die</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">! Check it out on </span><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/dodgy-diet/id1624599477\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">iOS</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and </span><a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=io.appstop.dodgydiet\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Android</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>"
